From ad39d9d1d09b61622c5caacccc49894aba8616db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bank-check-memo <none@invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:44:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_BANK_CHECK_MEMO=<microseconds>: a native bank
 compared in full that recently is not compared again at this bind (live
 switch; unset = every bind compares, as before); EDEN_UP_FRAME_COST counts
 and times the bank checks

EDEN_NX2_BANK_REUPLOAD=4 runs BufferCache::Nx2CheckBankPages at every bind of a 64 KiB native
bank: per page two device memory lookups, a hash map lookup and a 4 KiB memcmp, for every stage
of every draw that binds one. On a base PS5 (T120, Ocarina of Time, 13 Nov) the GPU profile put
150 to 190 ms a second in 'bind stage buffers', about 3 us a call at 50,000 to 60,000 calls a
second, the largest zone of the drawing thread after the methods. Whether that time is these
checks is what the new 'Frame cost (banks)' line says; it is not known yet.

With the switch a check is left out when all of the same bank (address, size, device memory
mapping) was compared less than the given time ago. Bytes the tracker missed that the game
wrote in between are found by the next check, at most that much later; the pages marked and
the test that marks them are unchanged. Forgetting the snapshots clears the memo, and
EDEN_NX2_BANK_STATS never skips.

- video_core/buffer_cache/bank_check_memo.h (new): the memo and the 5 s line, standard library
  only, tested off the console.
- common/live_switch.h: the switch (index 15), so a schedule can turn it on and off in a run.
- buffer_cache.h, buffer_cache_base.h: the memo around the check, the counters, the line.

Not run on a console.
